@@ -577,6 +577,70 @@
   Root/callee checksums, lexical checkpoint validation, and
   projection-integrity guards remain unchanged.
 
+## Derived Pure-Result Persistence Profile (`derived_pure_replay.v1`)
+
+`result_persistence_profile` is an optional, additive top-level field of the
+run state (schema stays `2.1`). Absent means the historical bundle-backed
+persistence; `to_dict()` omits the key and `from_dict()` of a payload without it
+yields `None`. The only supported value is `derived_pure_replay.v1`; any other
+value fails closed with a `ValueError` naming the profile at `RunState`
+construction, `StateManager.initialize(...)` and state load (a failed load
+leaves the state file unchanged). Ordinary loads never infer, backfill or
+upgrade the field.
+
+**Selection.** `StateManager.initialize(..., result_persistence_profile=None)`
+writes the field atomically when the state is created. `orchestrator run` of a
+compiled `.orc` workflow and the new root created by
+`orchestrator resume --force-restart` select the profile; the force-restart
+source run is left byte-for-byte unchanged. A fresh, non-iterative child call
+frame whose callee bundle has `frontend_kind == "workflow_lisp"` also selects it
+(from the callee's typed provenance only, never the parent's profile). A fresh
+retry after a failed Workflow Lisp predecessor is new state and selects it.
+Existing roots and frames, non-Workflow-Lisp callees and iteration-owned child
+frames keep the historical profile; an existing frame is never backfilled, and
+an existing frame without a mapping `state` is rejected (`existing call-frame
+state`) before anything is written.
+
+**Eligibility.** A compiler-generated `pure_projection` is replay-eligible when
+it is acyclic and visited at most once per scope. Recurrent, loop-owned and other
+multiply visited pure nodes (`multiple_visit_region`) keep full durable rows,
+bundles and checkpoints. `derive_pure_result_replay_index(bundle)` derives the
+eligible nodes, their typed binding addresses and their pure/durable dependency
+edges without mutating the bundle; refs are scoped to the workflow holding them.
+
+**Completion shell.** An eligible pure success persists exactly
+`{"name", "step_id", "visit_count": 1, "status": "completed", "exit_code": 0,
+"outcome": {"status": "completed", "phase": "execution", "class": "completed",
+"retryable": false}, "result_storage": "derived_pure_replay.v1"}` and nothing
+else. Failed and skipped rows stay full durable rows. No result bundle, private
+lineage (`private_artifact_versions`) or checkpoint record is written for an
+eligible node, and restore payloads omit derivable pure bindings. Visit start,
+cursor, shell/failure settlement are each one atomic state transaction
+(`begin_eligible_pure_visit`, `reuse_interrupted_eligible_pure_visit`,
+`settle_eligible_pure_success`, `settle_eligible_pure_failure`).
+
+**Progress classification.** For one witness `(presentation_key, step_index,
+step_id, visit_count)`: `unstarted` (no visit, cursor or row; an unrelated cursor
+is allowed), `interrupted` (visit + matching running cursor, no row),
+`derived_complete` (visit + exact shell), `durable_failure_skip` (visit + full
+failed/skipped row). Every other combination is `progress_witness_invalid`.
+
+**Resume.** Resume audits the persisted surfaces (`profile_conflict` for a value
+row, pure bundle, private lineage, checkpoint record or restore binding of an
+eligible node), validates progress witnesses and the durable dependency leaves of
+the required boundary, and rebuilds the needed pure values in an in-memory
+overlay by re-evaluating them; replay never dispatches an effect, increments a
+visit or writes state. Failures end the run before any effect with
+`error.type == "pure_result_replay_unavailable"` and `error.context.reason` one
+of `durable_input_missing`, `durable_input_invalid`, `binding_unresolved`,
+`evaluation_failed`, `output_contract_invalid`, `progress_witness_invalid`.
+Default resume admits one zero-record case, `VALIDATED_FRAME_ENTRY_REPLAY`
+(`selection_reason: validated_frame_entry_replay`), only when no durable effect
+boundary precedes the restart node and the bound-input leaves and progress
+witnesses validate; otherwise it fails closed with
+`lexical_default_resume_prior_boundary_not_restorable`. The restart boundary is
+determined once per resume and passed on to the default-resume decision.
+
 ## Reusable-Call State Contract (v2.5)
 
 - Caller-visible exports
